  "scene": {
    "id": "S1-conversational",
    "title": "Option 1 · Conversational Agent (PoC-equivalent)",
    "caption": "PoC-equivalent low-code path from the GenAiR low-code docs (Conversational Agents = renamed Dialogflow CX: generative playbook,\ndata store tool, Google Chat integration), the GenAiR template exports, the ARB deck (slides 2, 4) and the ARD (FP1–FP6).\nEmployees ask in a Google Chat space; the Chat integration (or, per ARD FP1, an Apps Script router) reaches an agent whose playbook\ngrounds Gemini answers on a Vertex AI Search data store fed from a GCS bucket (Phase 1 manual upload; Phase 2 Drive sync not built).\nTwo PoC Cloud Run tools are called from the playbook: Link Formatter and Row-Level Access Security (dormant); logs go to BigQuery (FP6).\nRed frames: no GenAiR production template, IaC or CI path for Conversational Agents (GenAiR-Cutter offers Cloud Run / Agent Engine only;\nconsole build and zip restore), the Dialogflow ↔ Chat connection was rejected in POD (`auth.creds.useNormalUserEUC`, handover §C,\nobserved with Dialogflow ES), the Apps Script route needs a VPC-SC ingress rule per user identity. The PoC agent export was not found: `source-gap`.\nInheritance and environments: the agent starts from the `genair-conversational-agent` exports of `Airbus/GenAiR` (github.airbus.corp). With no Cutter template, the PROD dev / int / pro projects (orange, GenAiR PROD model) would each receive a manual console restore of an export versioned on the Airbus SCM (GitLab or GitHub: open); no webhook, no Jenkins job and no IaC exist for this path. Project ids: unknown.",
    "legendPassages": [
      "Red frames: no GenAiR production template, IaC or CI path for Conversational Agents (GenAiR-Cutter offers Cloud Run / Agent Engine only; console build and zip restore), the Dialogflow ↔ Chat connection was rejected in POD (`auth.creds.useNormalUserEUC`, handover §C, observed with Dialogflow ES), the Apps Script route needs a VPC-SC ingress rule per user identity. The PoC agent export was not found: `source-gap`."
    ]
  },
